Here is a conversation I had a while ago with Mr. Farrer about galeon on the
alpha.

-----Original Message-----
From: 'Ron Farrer' [mailto:rbf@farrer.net]
Sent: Thursday, January 03, 2002 1:22 PM
To: Schroeder, Aaron
Subject: Re: Netscape on Alpha?


Schroeder, Aaron (Aaron.Schroeder@qg.com) wrote:

> I updated my sources.list and changed the stable to unstable and then did
a
> apt-get dist-upgrade, is that the proper way to do things? I am running
> Kernel 2.2.18pre21 as well, just in case you needed that info.
> 
> Ok, so I won't download the debs... :)

Here is what your sources.list should look like for unstable:

#Start here
deb http://http.us.debian.org/debian unstable main contrib non-free
non-free deb http://nonus.debian.org/debian-non-US unstable/non-US main
contrib
# This part is optional:
deb-src http://http.us.debian.org/debian unstable main contrib non-free
contrib non-free
deb-src http://nonus.debian.org/debian-non-US unstable/non-US main contrib
non-free
#end

Running unstable is your choice, but I personally run testing with some
unstable. My sources.list looks like:

# Start here
deb http://http.us.debian.org/debian testing main contrib non-free 
deb http://http.us.debian.org/debian unstable main contrib non-free
deb http://nonus.debian.org/debian-non-US testing/non-US main contrib
non-free
deb http://nonus.debian.org/debian-non-US unstable/non-US main contrib
non-free
# This part is optional:
deb-src http://http.us.debian.org/debian testing main contrib non-free
deb-src http://http.us.debian.org/debian unstable main contrib non-free
deb-src http://nonus.debian.org/debian-non-US testing/non-US main contrib
non-free
deb-src http://nonus.debian.org/debian-non-US unstable/non-US main contrib
non-free
#end

Then do:
apt-get clean
apt-get update
apt-get -f dist-upgrade

After that's all done, to install galeon do a:
apt-get -f --default-release unstable install galeon

HTH,
Ron


