Good system.  I use a 533 MHz LX daily as my primary machine.  While not=20
as zippy as the dual P4 on my desk at work, it holds its own quite well.

> * What PCI USB host controllers would work with Debian/Alpha?

I have a generic OHCI USB PCI card in my LX -- sorry don't remember the=20
brand.  I use it primarily for a CompactFlash reader (for a digital=20
camera).  Make sure you have a recent 2.4 kernel... there were quite a few=
=20
Alpha-specific bugs with early 2.4 USB support.  Support is still not what=
=20
I'd call flawless -- very few Alpha systems have USB ports.

> * Would any USB CD-RW supported by the 2.4 kernel be supported by
> Debian/Alpha?

I would think you're taking a big chance with USB CD-RW and Alpha... I=20
have a SCSI burner and it works fine; others I know use IDE w/o a problem=
=20
(though make sure you have the very latest SRM firmware for IDE to work=20
well).  If you already have the burner, give it a shot. Otherwise I'd=20
advise against it.

